            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We don't have any arrays of bools anymore, and this has been supported by the bindings for a while now, can we just make this common?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> We don't have any arrays of bools anymore\n\nHow do you know?\n\nEM configs are supposed to be a stable extension point for downstream, \nas you stated [here](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/79744/comments/4635f6e6_7f553143).\n\nThat's part of the reason why i could not drop support for arrays of EM configs.\n\nMaybe i am misunderstanding the code, but isn't this the code which puts the properties and values from the json configs on DBus?\n\nAny change to the type there could cause major problems in case there is any daemons (upstream or downstream) which rely on this EM quirk."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "Not exactly. \n\nThis adds the property/value to the dbus object in memory, but does not execute the placement directly. The `tryIfaceInitialize(iface)`-function places stuff on DBus."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Good to know \ud83d\udc4d\n\nI will close this discussion thread since i consider the quirk to be unavoidable for now. At some point in the future when the EM is cleaned up,\nthis quirk will attract more interest and people can begin their testing to see if there is anything which still requires this special case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> How do you know?\n\nAre there any schemas with array of bool?  I'm not aware of any.  I'm not asking to drop support for arrays, but arrays of bool should just be arrays of bools."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a really unfortunate variable name.  Can we come up with a better one?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "`AltPropertyType` or `AlternativePropertyType` maybe?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Renamed to ```SinglePropertyType``` since it's the case without the array."
                }
            ],
